  "label": "User projected onto the man as the speaker of the hateful message",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man, who is depicted as the speaker of the text 'I'm not racist, racism is a crime' and 'and crime is for them'. The man's defensive posture and facial expression, combined with the text, create an analogical mapping where the user identifies with or imagines themselves as the person making this statement. This projection is implicit, as the meme does not use explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the user is expected to see themselves in the role of the speaker, embodying the hateful trope.",
